# Frames for language (frames.ath is kept separate). See language/BASE.md and ontology/SOURCES.md.
check "python3 -I language/check.py"
seq parses = run "python3 -I language/check.py" "parse trees of x op x"
seq catalan = from brain/neuron/fingerprints.json "Catalan"
claim parses matches catalan
frame "Addison: prove what can be proved of language; the Chomsky hierarchy (language/BASE.md a)" reading "no DFA with <= 3 states over {a,b} agrees with a^n b^n on all strings of length <= 8; each k-state DFA, k=1..3, disagrees by length 2k-1 (worst cases 1, 2, 4); every k by the Myhill-Nerode reduction in BASE.md" -> 2 label checked-finite reach 2 cost 80
frame "Addison: grammars that count (language/BASE.md a)" reading "S -> (S)S | e generates exactly the balanced strings, Catalan(m) at length 2m for m=0..8, one parse each; S -> aSb | e one string per even length" -> 2 label checked-finite reach 1 cost 40
frame "Addison: ambiguity counted exactly (language/BASE.md b)" reading "E -> E+E | E*E | x gives Catalan(n) parse trees to every sentence with n operators, n=0..8; the precedence grammar gives exactly 1" -> 2 label checked-finite reach 2 cost 40
frame "Montague 1973, The proper treatment of quantification in ordinary English (not re-read): scope ambiguity (language/BASE.md c)" reading "every student reads some book has two readings; they differ on a model of size 1 (and of size 2 with students and books); the inverse reading implies the surface one on all 33032 models of size 1..3" -> 2 label checked-finite reach 2 cost 80
frame "Addison: ambiguity as qual-quant, a sentence that means more than one thing has a count (ontology/QUALQUANT.md)" reading "the count of readings: 1 for every..every and some..some, 2 for mixed quantifiers, on models of size 1..3; Catalan(n) parse trees for n operators" -> 2 label checked-finite reach 2 cost 40
frame "brain/neuron ordered arbor shapes as parse trees (neuron.ath)" reading "parse trees of x+...+x with n+1 leaves, operators erased, are exactly the ordered binary arbor shapes with n+1 tips, n=0..6; the counts match the brain Catalan fingerprint" -> 5 label checked-finite reach 2 cost 40
# Stays open: no theorem about natural language as a whole is claimed here.
frame "Addison: what can be proved of natural language in general" reading "a finite fragment is all that is checked; English is not a formal language with a fixed grammar here" -> none label open reach 1 cost 160
record language chomsky checked-finite "frames_language.ath: language/check.py passes. No DFA with <= 3 states over {a,b} accepts exactly a^n b^n on the 511 strings of length <= 8; the worst first disagreement over k-state DFAs is 1, 2, 4 for k=1..3 (bound 2k-1). Distinct languages up to length 8: 2, 26, 1054. S -> (S)S | e gives Catalan(m) balanced strings at length 2m, m=0..8, unambiguously."
record language ambiguity checked-finite "frames_language.ath: under E -> E+E | E*E | x every sentence with n operators has Catalan(n) parse trees, n=0..8 (chart count; explicit enumeration n<=6); the precedence grammar gives exactly 1. Parse-tree shapes with n+1 leaves equal brain/neuron's ordered arbor shapes, n=0..6."
record language scope checked-finite "frames_language.ath: every student reads some book has two readings; on all 33032 models with domain size 1..3 the inverse reading implies the surface one, and they differ (smallest: one element, no students, no books; with both non-empty: domain 2, reads = {(0,1),(1,0)}). Same quantifiers give one reading."
